      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This study elucidates that modulating the pKa of ionizable lipid headgroups within lipid nanoparticle (LNP) formulations significantly enhances endosomal escape kinetics in murine hepatocytes. Concurrently, optimizing the nitrogen-to-phosphate (N/P) stoichiometry maximizes hepatic translational efficiency, while the incorporation of pseudouridine-modified nucleosides effectively dampens interferon-inducing cytokine signaling through the suppression of TLR7 and TLR8 activation. These synergistic molecular engineering strategies collectively result in reduced innate immune activation, thereby establishing a foundation for dosing regimens that minimize adverse inflammatory responses while sustaining high levels of antigenic protein secretion.",
      "source": "target",
