      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start and it's definitely accurate. i just ran it through the internal checker and the term density score is actually a bit lower than what we usually need for these deep-dives. the supervisor is really picky about these being \"high-density\" technical reports.\n\ncould you expand on this? go into more detail regarding the molecular mechanisms mentioned—like the specific pathways or the biochemical implications of the N/P ratio and the lipid modifications. try to push the technical density a bit higher so we hit that target score, but again, please keep it a coherent, scientifically rigorous summary. don't just list terms, make sure it actually explains the process thoroughly.",
